IMPORT prelude

-- Parking Places (Surcharge) Act 1975 (Singapore) -- the whole Act: what a parking place is (s 2), when the surcharge is
-- levied and payable and when it may be refunded (s 3), the duty to give forms and returns and the offence (s 4),
-- composition (s 5), the Minister's exemption (s 7) and the exclusion of private house parking (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PPSA1975.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021.
-- The latest amendment annotated in the body is [24/2018] on s 8(1); the Legislative History lists Act 24 of 2018
-- (Parking Places (Amendment) Act 2018, s 20), commenced 1 May 2018.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone who owns or runs a car park of five or more lots in a
-- designated area -- a shop, an office building, a condominium, a statutory board -- may owe this surcharge, and the price
-- of parking there may carry it. Not chosen by citation count. The Act is nine sections long, so it is encoded whole,
-- except ss 1, 6 (payment into the Consolidated Fund) and 9 (rules), which carry no rule a person meets.
--
-- NOT ENCODED, because the Act does not contain it: which areas are designated, the surcharge rates, and when and how it
-- is paid. All three are left to Ministerial orders in the Gazette (ss 2, 3(1)-(3)), none of which was retrieved. No
-- exemption order under s 7 was retrieved either.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parking Places (Surcharge) Act 1975`

§§ `2 -- parking place`

-- s 2: "'parking place' means any land or premises, or any part of the land or premises, owned by any person, statutory
-- board or institution and used for the parking of 5 OR MORE MOTOR VEHICLES"; "'motor vehicle' means a mechanically
-- propelled vehicle intended or adapted for use on roads"; "'parking lot' means the space marked out in a parking place for
-- the parking of one motor vehicle".
--
-- The count is of motor vehicles. Bicycles are not mechanically propelled, so a bicycle rack is not a parking place however
-- large (an inference from the definition). Four cars do not make a parking place; five do.
DECLARE `Car park` HAS
    `motor vehicles it is used to park` IS A NUMBER
    `in a designated area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a private parking place used exclusively with a private dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `vehicles kept for private use only` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the car park` IS A `Car park`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the car park is a parking place` IF
    `the car park`'s `motor vehicles it is used to park` AT LEAST 5

§§ `8 -- private house parking`

-- s 8(1): "The provisions of this Act do not apply to private parking places used EXCLUSIVELY in connection with any private
-- dwelling house for the housing or parking of vehicles kept for PRIVATE USE ONLY." [24/2018]
-- s 8(2): "'dwelling house' means any building or tenement, or any part thereof, which is used, constructed or adapted for
-- use for human habitation."
--
-- All three limbs are needed: private, exclusively for a dwelling house, and private-use vehicles only. A house whose drive
-- also takes a business's vans is caught. The definition of dwelling house is not limited to a detached house; whether a
-- condominium's residents' car park falls within s 8 the text does not say outright, and this encoding treats it as a fact
-- the user supplies.
GIVEN `the car park` IS A `Car park`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the car park` IF
    NOT (    `the car park`'s `a private parking place used exclusively with a private dwelling house`
         AND `the car park`'s `vehicles kept for private use only`)

§§ `3(1), 7 -- the levy`

-- s 3(1): "There is to be levied a surcharge in respect of EVERY parking place in any designated area at such rate or rates
-- as the Minister may, by order in the Gazette, determine." s 2: a designated area is any area the Minister specifies by
-- order in the Gazette.
-- s 7: "The Minister may exempt any parking place or part of any parking place from all or any of the provisions of this Act."
GIVEN `the car park` IS A `Car park`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge is levied` IF
        `the car park is a parking place` `the car park`
    AND `the car park`'s `in a designated area`
    AND (NOT `the car park`'s `exempted by the Minister`)
    AND `the Act applies to the car park` `the car park`

§§ `3(2) -- the basis of the rate`

-- s 3(2): "Such rate or rates must be on the basis of the number of parking lots OR OTHERWISE as the Minister may determine."
--
-- The Act fixes no rate. This function shows only the per-lot basis the Act names, with the rate as an input; whether the
-- current order uses it, and at what rate, was not retrieved.
GIVEN `number of lots` IS A NUMBER, `rate per lot` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the surcharge on a per-lot basis` IS
    `number of lots` TIMES `rate per lot`

§§ `3(3)-(6) -- payment and refund`

-- s 3(3): payable "at such time and in such manner as the Minister may, by order in the Gazette, determine".
-- s 3(4): "The surcharge is payable, WITHOUT DEMAND, at the office of the Superintendent or any other prescribed place."
-- s 3(5): recoverable "as a debt due to the Government".
-- s 3(6): "Despite the provisions of any other written law, the Superintendent MUST NOT refund any surcharge EXCEPT in such
-- special circumstances as the Superintendent may approve."
--
-- No demand, no bill: the surcharge falls due when the time comes whether or not anyone asks for it.
GIVEN `levied` IS A BOOLEAN, `the time fixed for payment has come` IS A BOOLEAN, `a demand was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge is due` IF
    `levied` AND `the time fixed for payment has come`

GIVEN `paid in error or overpaid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Superintendent approves special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Superintendent may refund` IF
    `the Superintendent approves special circumstances`

§§ `4 -- forms, returns and information`

-- s 4(1): the Superintendent may require any person "(a) to submit or give ... any form, return OR INFORMATION; or (b) to
-- answer any question raised by the Superintendent".
-- s 4(3): "Any person who fails to submit any FORM OR RETURN as required under subsection (1), or who in any such form or
-- return makes any statement which is false in any MATERIAL particular, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 OR to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months."
--
-- s 4(3) names forms and returns only. Failing to give information or to answer a question, though the Superintendent may
-- require both, is not within its words. Nor does s 4(3) require that the false statement be made knowingly: on its face
-- a material falsehood suffices.
DECLARE Default IS ONE OF
    `failing to submit a required form`
    `failing to submit a required return`
    `a statement false in a material particular in a form or return`
    `a statement false in an immaterial particular`
    `failing to give required information`
    `failing to answer the Superintendent's question`

GIVEN `the default` IS A Default
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the default is an offence under section 4(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the default`
    WHEN `failing to submit a required form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `failing to submit a required return` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statement false in a material particular in a form or return` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The penalty is a fine OR imprisonment, not both.
GIVEN `fine imposed` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within section 4(3)` IF
        (`fine imposed` AT MOST 5000 AND `months of imprisonment imposed` EQUALS 0)
    OR  (`fine imposed` EQUALS 0 AND `months of imprisonment imposed` AT MOST 6)

§§ `5 -- composition`

-- s 5: the Superintendent "may accept from any person who is REASONABLY SUSPECTED of having committed an offence under this
-- Act or any of its orders or rules a sum of money NOT EXCEEDING $500 by way of composition".
GIVEN `reasonably suspected of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Superintendent may accept the composition` IF
    `reasonably suspected of an offence` AND `sum offered` AT MOST 500
